      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Approximately 100 wallets hold roughly 89% of Canton Coin supply, creating acute concentration risk for a network marketing itself on institutional trust and broad participation.",
          "source": "https://fr.tradingview.com/news/stocktwits:108cd7392094b:0-grayscale-files-for-canton-etf-targeting-a-token-where-100-wallets-hold-89-of-supply/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart Contract / Protocol",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "DAML-based contracts reduce common EVM attack vectors, but Canton-specific logic handling $6T+ in tokenized RWA carries unquantified tail risk with limited public audit history relative to battle-tested EVM environments.",
          "source": "https://www.canton.network/blog/a-technical-primer"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The permissioned-validator architecture is designed for compliance, but concurrent tokenization of U.S. Treasuries, UK Gilts, and Swiss-custody assets exposes Canton to fragmented and still-evolving cross-jurisdictional securities regulation.",
          "source": "https://www.dtcc.com/news/2025/december/17/dtcc-and-digital-asset-partner-to-tokenize-dtc-custodied-us-treasury-securities"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Governance / Capture",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The GlobalSyncFdn has grown to 30+ members including HSBC and BNP Paribas, but founding institutional validators retain outsized influence, creating governance capture risk if large participants align against smaller network members.",
          "source": "https://canton.foundation/validators/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Retail depth for CC remains thin despite AMINA's FINMA-regulated custody launch; supply concentration and an institutionally gated validator structure structurally limit open-market liquidity.",
          "source": "https://zenith.network/resources/blog/understanding-canton-1-canton-coin-economics-burn-mint-equilibrium"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / Valuation",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "CC's outperformance during broader crypto stress reflects speculative positioning on institutional adoption timelines; if DTCC or other flagship deployments slip, the thesis-driven premium unwinds faster than underlying network utility would justify.",
          "source": "https://blog.digitalasset.com/press-release/digital-asset-355m-funding-canton-capital-markets"
        }
      ],
